          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "The Skyrme theory has a rich topological structure. It has skyrmion and baby skyrmion \\cite{skyrme,piet}. But recently it has been shown that the theory allows a knotted soliton identical to the Faddeev-Niemi knot in Skyrme-Faddeev non-linear sigma model, which can be identified as a twisted vortex ring made of helical baby skyrmion \\cite{prl01,plb04}. To see this, we review the knot in Skyrme theory first. Let",
      "extractCut": true
