        }
      ],
      "extract": "In the above gauge theory of spin-1/2 condensates the gauge interaction was a self-induced interaction. But when the doublet is charged, the gauge interaction can be treated as independent. In this case the theory can describe a two-gap superconductor. But even in this case the knot topology and thus the knot itself should survive. This implies that two-gap superconductor should also have a topological knot. The",
